# Code owners for shirabe.
#
# An entry here means a PR touching the matched paths cannot merge without the
# named owner's review. Owners must be a GitHub user or a team with write
# access on this repository; an owner GitHub cannot resolve is silently
# ignored, which turns the control off without saying so.

# The tool-diagnostic discard enumeration gates CI. Anything listed in it is a
# call site allowed to throw away a tool's diagnostic output, and the claim
# that adding one "costs a reviewed edit" is a claim about a process -- a
# process with no owner is not a control. `shirabe#279` was silent because
# whoever wrote that call site decided on their own that the fallback was not a
# masked failure. This line is what makes that decision somebody else's to
# approve.
# @dangazineu is used rather than a team handle because an owner GitHub
# cannot resolve is silently ignored, which turns this control off without
# reporting anything. This handle was verified to resolve as a collaborator.
# Replace it with a team once that team is confirmed to exist.
